            misconception:
                "Fasting is not hatred of the body, a weight-loss program, a proof of holiness, or permission to ignore medical needs. Feasting is not baptized excess. Catholic discipline includes real communal obligations and legitimate exemptions; personal practices require prudence. Eating disorders, food insecurity, pregnancy, illness, medication, and other vulnerabilities call for appropriate adaptation, assistance, and qualified guidance. A safer alternative penance is not second-class discipleship when it preserves the purposes of conversion, prayer, mercy, and freedom. The Church's communal discipline should be learned accurately rather than intensified through rumor or comparison.",
