            caseStudy:
                "A man repeatedly gambles online after stressful workdays, hides losses, and promises his spouse he can stop without help. He prays after each episode but refuses financial safeguards because they feel humiliating. The household is now missing bill payments. Distinguish the good of repentance from secrecy, the spouse's right to safety and truth, possible diminished control, restitution, professional assessment, financial protection, and spiritual care. What immediate and long-term layers are needed?",
